sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Client as Tenant or Operator
    participant API as Control API
    participant DB as State and Outbox
    participant Kafka as Versioned Kafka Topics
    participant Orch as Orchestrator
    participant Port as Provider gRPC Port
    participant Adapter as Provider Adapter
    participant Reconciler

    Client->>API: REST or gRPC command with auth, idempotency, trace context
    API->>DB: Atomically commit desired state, operation, and outbox event
    API-->>Client: 202 Accepted and operation identity
    DB-)Kafka: Debezium publishes command envelope v1
    Kafka-)Orch: At-least-once command keyed by aggregateId
    Orch->>Orch: Deduplicate eventId and claim workflow checkpoint
    Orch->>Port: Provider-neutral RPC with requestId and deadline
    Port->>Adapter: Translate domain values into provider API calls
    Adapter-->>Port: Accepted, rejected, succeeded, or unknown outcome
    Port-->>Orch: Normalized result, task reference, and safe evidence ID
    Orch->>DB: Commit checkpoint, inbox receipt, and event outbox
    DB-)Kafka: Publish workflow fact with propagated trace context
    Kafka-)API: Apply idempotent read projection update

    alt Provider result is conclusive
        Client->>API: Read operation or instance
        API-->>Client: Current desired and observed state
    else Provider result is ambiguous
        Orch->>DB: Persist UNKNOWN_OUTCOME and stop blind retries
        Reconciler->>Port: Observe resource using ownership markers
        Port-->>Reconciler: Verified observation or inconclusive evidence
        Reconciler->>DB: Resolve outcome or create manual review
    end

    Note over Client,Reconciler: W3C trace context crosses every boundary.<br/>Fields marked prohibited never enter telemetry.
